CHOWN(1)                    User Commands

NAME
    chown, chgrp - change the owner and group of files

SYNOPSIS
    chown [-R] [-h] owner[:group] file...
    chown [-R] [-h] :group file...
    chgrp [-R] [-h] group file...

DESCRIPTION
    chown sets the owner, and with :group also the group, of each file.
    owner: with an empty group sets the login group of owner from
    /etc/passwd, and :group alone changes only the group. chgrp changes
    the group. Owners and groups are names of /etc/passwd and /etc/group
    or numbers.

    -R changes directories and everything below them, changing symbolic
    links met during the walk themselves. -h changes a symbolic link named
    on the command line itself instead of the file it leads to.

    Only root may change the owner. The owner of a file may change its
    group to one of the groups the owner belongs to. A change made by
    anyone but root clears the set user id and set group id bits of a file.

SEE ALSO
    chmod(1), id(1), ls(1), passwd(5), index(7)
